<section class="section container"><div class="section-header"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start here</span><h2 class="display-heading">What do you <em>need help with?</em></h2></div></div><div class="three-link-grid"><a href="#accounts-help"><span aria-hidden="true">◫</span><h3>Accounts</h3><p>Balances, transactions and access to your account.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↘</b></a><a href="#cards-help"><span aria-hidden="true">▣</span><h3>Cards</h3><p>Card use, keeping details safe and reporting concerns.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↘</b></a><a href="/locations"><span aria-hidden="true">⌖</span><h3>Visit us</h3><p>Find a branch or ATM that works for you.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div></section>
<section class="section soft-section"><div class="container faq-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</span><h2 class="display-heading">Answers for <em>everyday life.</em></h2><p>Explore common questions about your accounts, cards and online banking.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><h3 id="accounts-help">Accounts &amp; online banking</h3><details><summary>Where can I check my account balance?</summary><p>Use online banking to see your available balance and recent account activity.</p></details><details><summary>How do I review recent transactions?</summary><p>Open your account overview in online banking to review recent deposits and payments.</p></details><details><summary>What should I do if I do not recognise a transaction?</summary><p>Contact the bank through your usual verified channel or visit a branch as soon as possible. Do not share your password, PIN or one-time code.</p></details><h3 id="cards-help">Cards &amp; security</h3><details><summary>How do I keep my card information safe?</summary><p>Keep your PIN private, check your card activity regularly and avoid sharing card details through unverified messages or websites.</p></details><details><summary>What if my card is lost or stolen?</summary><p>Contact the bank through a verified service channel immediately to request assistance with your card.</p></details><details><summary>Will the bank ask me for a one-time code?</summary><p>Never share one-time codes, passwords or PINs with anyone who contacts you unexpectedly.</p></details></div></div></section>
